/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Remove Nth Node From End of List
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Linked List
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given the head of a linked list, remove the nth node from the
end of the list and return the head of the modified list.

Approach:
Use two pointers along with a dummy node.

The first pointer is moved n + 1 positions ahead of the
second pointer. This creates a gap of n nodes between them.

Then move both pointers together until the first pointer
reaches the end of the list. At that point, the second pointer
will be positioned immediately before the node that needs to
be removed.

A dummy node is used before the head so that the same logic
works even when the first node needs to be deleted.

Why does this work?

The fixed gap of n nodes between the two pointers ensures that
when the first pointer reaches the end, the second pointer is
exactly at the node before the target node.

This allows the target node to be removed in a single traversal
without calculating the length of the linked list first.

Algorithm:
1. Create a dummy node pointing to the head.
2. Initialize two pointers at the dummy node.
3. Move the first pointer n + 1 positions forward.
4. Move both pointers until the first pointer reaches the end.
5. The second pointer is now before the node to remove.
6. Store the node to be deleted.
7. Skip the target node.
8. Delete the removed node.
9. Return the node after the dummy node.

Time Complexity : O(n)

Reason:
The linked list is traversed only once.

Space Complexity : O(1)

Reason:
Only a constant number of pointers are used.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* removeNthFromEnd(ListNode* head, int n) {

        // Dummy node handles the case where the head is removed.
        ListNode* dummy = new ListNode(0, head);

        ListNode* fast = dummy;
        ListNode* slow = dummy;

        // Create a gap of n nodes between fast and slow.
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
            fast = fast->next;
        }

        // Move both pointers until fast reaches the end.
        while (fast != nullptr) {
            fast = fast->next;
            slow = slow->next;
        }

        // The node after slow is the node to be removed.
        ListNode* nodeToDelete = slow->next;

        // Remove the target node from the linked list.
        slow->next = slow->next->next;

        // Free the removed node.
        delete nodeToDelete;

        // Return the actual head, skipping the dummy node.
        ListNode* newHead = dummy->next;

        // Free the dummy node.
        delete dummy;

        return newHead;
    }
};
